{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' __issue_context__.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"body\": \"Please check that the term does not already exist by using the ontology search tool OLS:\\nhttps://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl\\n\\n\\n**Preferred term label**\\nUnclassified Fallopian Tube Progenitor (UCFP)\\n\\n**Synonyms** (add reference(s), please)\\nPrior work (PMID: 35320732) has referred to similar UCFP cells as clusters 2-1 and 2-2 that can give rise to epithelial and endothelial/stromal cell types through scRNA-seq and trajectory inference.\\n\\n**Definition** (free text, with reference(s), please. PubMed ID format is PMID:XXXXXX)\\nWe propose a new, broad definition for the observed \\\"dual-feature\\\" human fallopian tube progenitor-like cells that simultaneously express epithelial (e.g., EpCAM/CD326) and endothelial (e.g., PECAM1/CD31) markers, both on the cell surface and by RNA expression that can give rise to ciliated and secretory cell types, and potentially to endothelial/stromal cell types. These \\\"dual-feature\\\" unclassified fallopian tube progenitor cells have primary been observed by single-cell RNA-seq (scRNA-seq), flow cytometry, and immunofluorescence, with the UCFP term proposed in PMID: 40475517.\\n\\n**Parent cell type term** (check the hierarchy here https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/cl)\\nI am not entirely sure as these could exist under CL:4052019 or CL:4052018. \\n\\n**Anatomical structure where the cell type is found** (check Uberon for anatomical structures: https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/ontologies/uberon)\\nHuman fallopian tube\\n\\n**Your ORCID**\\n0000-0002-1482-1032\\n\\n**Additional notes or concerns**\\nI'm sure this is incomplete and is my first attempt at this :) Thank you and my apologies in advance!\\n\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-863P-Pz\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"dosumis\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"CONTRIBUTOR\",\n      \"body\": \"Looks good, but would prefer something like 'dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell' as a name. I guess 'unclassified' is historical at this point - you just classified it.\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-07-15T16:55:22Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": true,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [],\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3196#issuecomment-3074417651\",\n      \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-8680l9V\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Caroline-99\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n      \"body\": \"Discussion with Ben: He is happy with us using `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell` as the main label in CL.\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-08-08T13:26:04Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [],\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3196#issuecomment-3167903573\",\n      \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOAjLh-869i1dc\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"Caroline-99\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"COLLABORATOR\",\n      \"body\": \"**Updates on text and logical defs (have been reviewed by @biobenkj ):**\\n\\n**label**\\ndual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell\\n\\n**textual definition**\\n\\nA bipotent progenitor cell within the human fallopian tube epithelium, characterized by the concurrent expression of epithelial (e.g., EpCAM/CD326) and endothelial (e.g., PECAM1/CD31) markers at both the cell surface and transcript levels. This cell has the capacity to differentiate into ciliated and secretory epithelial cells, as well as potentially endothelial/stromal lineages. Positioned at the apex of lineage bifurcation, the cell exhibits stem-like and endothelial features, representing an intermediate developmental state between undifferentiated progenitors and lineage-committed epithelial cells.\\n\\n PMID: [40475517](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40475517/)\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\n\\nnon-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-1 (NCSE2-1 cells) - related synonym -  PMID: [35320732](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35320732/)\\nnon-ciliated secretory epithelial cell 2-2 (NCSE2-2 cells) - related synonym -  PMID: [35320732](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/35320732/)\\nunclassified fallopian tube progenitors - exact-  PMID: [40475517](https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/40475517/)\\n\\n**Logical definition:**\\n\\n'progenitor cell'\\n'part of' some 'fallopian tube epithelium'\\n'in taxon' some 'Homo sapiens'\\n'develops into' some 'fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell'\\n'develops into' some 'fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell'\\n\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2025-08-12T16:02:12Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": true,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [],\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3196#issuecomment-3180025692\",\n      \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"title\": \"[NTR] Unclassified Fallopian Tube Progenitor (UCFP)\",\n  \"url\": \"https://github.com/obophenotype/cell-ontology/issues/3196\"\n}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
