ive, CD117-negative, and CD161 negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000825 \"natural killer cell progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12633665\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18432934\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000826 \"A progenitor cell of the B cell lineage, with some lineage specific activity such as early stages of recombination of B cell receptor genes, but not yet fully committed to the B cell lineage until the expression of PAX5 occurs.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000826 \"progenitor B cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000826 \"progenitor B lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000826 \"progenitor B-cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000826 \"progenitor B-lymphocyte\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0781735149\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000827 \"A lymphoid progenitor cell of the T cell lineage, with some lineage specific marker expression, but not yet fully committed to the T cell lineage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000827 \"progenitor T cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7758949\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000828 \"A progenitor cell of the thrombocyte, a nucleated blood cell involved in coagulation typically seen in birds and other non-mammalian vertebrates.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000831 (mast cell progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1183570\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:8629001\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354811\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.copewithcytokines.de\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000831 \"A progenitor cell of the mast cell lineage. Markers for this cell are FceRIa-low, CD117-positive, CD9-positive, T1/ST2-positive, SCA1-negative, and lineage-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000831 \"mast cell progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000834 (neutrophil progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000834 \"A progenitor cell of the neutrophil lineage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000834 \"neutrophil progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000837 (hematopoietic multipotent progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000837 \"A hematopoietic multipotent progenitor cell is multipotent, but not capable of long-term self-renewal. These cells are characterized as lacking lineage cell surface markers and being CD34-positive in both mice and humans.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000837 \"hemopoietic progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000837 \"hematopoietic multipotent progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000838 (lymphoid lineage restricted progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000838 \"A progenitor cell restricted to the lymphoid lineage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000838 \"lymphoid progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000838 \"lymphoid lineage restricted progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000839 (myeloid lineage restricted progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000839 \"A progenitor cell restricted to the myeloid lineage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000839 \"myeloid progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000839 \"myeloid lineage restricted progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000894 \"DN1 thymic progenitor T cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000936 (early lymphoid progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000936 \"A lymphoid progenitor cell that is found in bone marrow, gives rise to B cells, T cells, natural killer cells and dendritic cells, and has the phenotype Lin-negative, Kit-positive, Sca-1-positive, FLT3-positive, CD34-positive, CD150 negative, and GlyA-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000936 \"lymphoid-primed multipotent progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000936 \"early lymphoid progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0000995 (CD34-positive, CD38-positive common myeloid progenitor OR CD34-positive, CD38-positive common lymphoid progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0000995 \"CD34-positive, CD38-positive common myeloid progenitor OR CD34-positive, CD38-positive common lymphoid progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001012 (CD7-negative lymphoid progenitor OR granulocyte monocyte progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001012 \"CD7-negative lymphoid progenitor OR granulocyte monocyte progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001019 (CD115-positive monocyte OR common dendritic progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001019 \"CD115-positive monocyte OR common dendritic progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001021 (CD34-positive, CD38-positive common lymphoid progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2346585\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001021 \"A common lymphoid progenitor that is CD10-positive, CD45RA-positive, CD34-positive and CD38-positive.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0001021 \"CD10-positive common lymphocyte progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0001021 \"These markers are associated with human common lymphoid progenitors. Originally described in the dendritic cell ontology (DC_CL:0000032)(PMID:19243617).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001021 \"CD34-positive, CD38-positive common lymphoid progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001023 (Kit-positive, CD34-positive common myeloid progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:1261582\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17952047\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001023 \"A common myeloid progenitor that is Kit-positive and CD34-positive, Il7ra-negative, and is SCA1-low and Fcgr2-low and Fcgr3-low.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001023 \"Kit-positive, CD34-positive common myeloid progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001025 (Kit-positive, Sca1-positive common lymphoid progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17952047\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001025 \"A common lymphoid progenitor that is Kit-low, FLT3-positive, IL7ralpha-positive, and SCA1-low.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0001025 \"CD217-positive common lymphocyte progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001025 \"Kit-positive, Sca1-positive common lymphoid progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001026 (CD34-positive, CD38-positive common myeloid progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2626675\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001026 \"A common myeloid progenitor that is CD34-positive, CD38-positive, IL3ra-low, CD10-negative, CD7-negative, CD45RA-negative, and IL-5Ralpha-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001026 \"CD34-positive, CD38-positive common myeloid progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001027 (CD7-negative lymphoid progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001027 \"CD7-negative lymphoid progenitor cell is a lymphoid progenitor cell that is CD34-positive, CD7-negative and CD45RA-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001027 \"CD7-negative lymphoid progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001028 (CD7-positive lymphoid progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19491395\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001028 \"CD7-positive lymphoid progenitor cell is a lymphoid progenitor cell that is CD34-positive, CD7-positive and is CD45RA-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001028 \"CD7-positive lymphoid progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001029 (common dendritic progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:amm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17922016\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19286519\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001029 \"Common dendritic precursor is a hematopoietic progenitor cell that is CD117-low, CD135-positive, CD115-positive and lacks plasma membrane parts for hematopoietic lineage markers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001029 \"common dendritic progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001030 (CD117-positive common myeloid progenitor OR CD217-positive common lymphoid progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001030 \"CD117-positive common myeloid progenitor OR CD217-positive common lymphoid progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001059 (common myeloid progenitor, CD34-positive)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:dsd\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0878932437\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2212039\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10724173\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16551251\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16647566\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001059 \"A progenitor cell committed to myeloid lineage, including the megakaryocyte and erythroid lineages. These cells are CD34-positive, and express Gata1, Gata2, C/EBPa, and Pu.1.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001059 \"common myeloid progenitor, CD34-positive\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001060 (hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell, lineage-negative)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001060 \"A hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell that has the ability to differentiate into limited cell types but lacks lineage cell markers and self renewal capabilities. Cell lacks hematopoeitic lineage markers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001060 \"hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell, lineage-negative\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0001066 (erythroid progenitor cell, mammalian)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721601464\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001066 \"A progenitor cell committed to the erythroid lineage. This cell is ter119-positive but lacks expression of other hematopoietic lineage markers (lin-negative).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0001066 \"erythroid progenitor cell, mammalian\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:cvs\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ymb\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22796012\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25851693\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0001070 \"An adipocyte that is beige in color, thermogenic, and which differentiates in white fat tissue from a Myf5-negative progenitor.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002000 (Kit-positive erythroid progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19805084\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002000 \"An erythroid progenitor cell is Kit-positive, Ly6A-negative, CD41-negative, CD127-negative, and CD123-negative. This cell type is also described as being lin-negative, Kit-positive, CD150-negative, CD41-negative, CD105-positive, and FcgR-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002000 \"c- Kit-positive erythroid progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002000 \"Kit-positive erythroid progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002001 (CD34-positive, CD38-positive granulocyte monocyte progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12615892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002001 \"A granulocyte monocyte progenitor is CD34-positive, CD38-positive, IL-3receptor-alpha-positive and is CD45RA-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002001 \"CD34-positive, CD38-positive granulocyte monocyte progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002002 (Kit-positive granulocyte monocyte progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12615892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16322423\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19273628\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002002 \"A granulocyte monocyte progenitor that is Kit-positive, CD34-positive, Fc-gamma receptor II/II-positive, and is Sca-1-negative, Il7ra-negative, Cxc3r1-negative, and CD90-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002002 \"Kit-positive granulocyte monocyte progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002003 (CD34-positive, GlyA-negative erythroid progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19621348\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002003 \"An erythroid progenitor cell that is CD34-positive and is GlyA-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002003 \"CD34-positive, GlyA-negative erythroid progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002005 (CD34-positive, CD38-positive megakaryocyte erythroid progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12615892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:190227700\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002005 \"A megakaryocyte erythroid progenitor cell is CD34-positive, CD38-positive and is IL3-receptor alpha-negative and CD45RA-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002005 \"CD34-positive, CD38-positive megakaryocyte erythroid progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002006 (Kit-positive, CD34-negative megakaryocyte erythroid progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12615892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://www.immgen.org/index_content.html\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002006 \"A megakaryocyte erythroid progenitor cell that is Kit-positive and is Sca1-negative, CD34-negative, CD90-negative, IL7r-alpha-negative and Fcgr II/III-low.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002006 \"Kit-positive, CD34-negative megakaryocyte erythroid progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002007 (Kit-low, CD34-positive eosinophil progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17582345\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002007 \"A lineage marker-negative, CD34-positive, IL5r-alpha-positive, and Sca1-negative eosinophil progenitor cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002007 \"Kit-low, CD34-positive eosinophil progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002008 (CD34-positive, CD38-positive eosinophil progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC2626675\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002008 \"A lineage marker-negative, CD34-positive, CD38-positive, IL3r-alpha-positive, IL5r-alpha-positive, and CD45RA-negative eosinophil progenitor cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002008 \"CD34-positive, CD38-positive eosinophil progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002009 (macrophage dendritic cell progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19273628\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002009 \"A progenitor cell that can give rise to plasmacytoid and myeloid dendritic cells, and to monocytes and macrophages.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002009 \"macrophage dendritic cell progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002011 (Kit-positive macrophage dendritic cell progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19273628\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002011 \"A progenitor cell that can give rise to plasmacytoid and myeloid dendritic cells, and to monocytes and macrophages. Marker for this cell is Kit-high, CD115-positive, CD135-positive, Cx3cr1-positive, and is Il7ra-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002011 \"Kit-positive macrophage dendritic cell progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002023 (CD34-positive, CD41-positive, CD42-positive megakaryocyte progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15232614\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002023 \"A megakaroycotye progenitor cell that is CD34-positive, CD41-positive and CD42-positive on the cell surface.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002023 \"CD34-positive, CD41-positive, CD42-positive megakaryocyte progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002024 (Kit-positive megakaryocyte progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16951553\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002024 \"A megakaryocyte progenitor cell that is Kit-positive, CD41-positive, CD9-positive, Sca-1-negative, IL7ralpha-negative, CD150-negative, and Fcgamma receptor II/III-low.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002024 \"Kit-positive megakaryocyte progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002025 (CD34-positive, CD41-positive, CD42-negative megakaryocyte progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15232614\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002025 \"A megakaryocyte progenitor cell that is CD34-positive, CD41-positive, and CD42-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002025 \"CD34-positive, CD41-positive, CD42-negative megakaryocyte progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15232614\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002026 \"A megakaryocyte progenitor cell that is CD34-negative, CD41-positive and CD42-positive.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002028 (basophil mast progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002028 \"basophil mast progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002029 (Fc-epsilon RIalpha-low mast cell progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002029 \"A lineage-negative, Kit-positive, CD45-positive mast cell progenitor that is Fc-epsilon RIalpha-low.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002029 \"Fc-epsilon RIalpha-low mast cell progenitor\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002030 (Fc-epsilon RIalpha-high basophil progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMCID:PMC1312421\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002030 \"A lineage negative, Sca1-negative basophil progenitor cell that is Fc epsilon RIalpha-high.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002030 \"Fc-epsilon RIalpha-high basophil progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002031 (hematopoietic lineage restricted progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002031 \"A hematopoietic progenitor cell that is capable of developing into only one lineage of hematopoietic cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002031 \"hematopoietic lineage restricted progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002032 (hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-5208-3432\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002032 \"A hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell that has the ability to differentiate into limited cell types but lacks lineage cell markers and self renewal capabilities.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002032 \"This cell type is intended to be compatible with any vertebrate hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell.  For mammalian hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cells known to be lineage-negative, please use the term 'hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell' (CL_0001060).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002032 \"hematopoietic oligopotent progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15572596\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002033 \"A hematopoietic stem cell capable of rapid replenishment of myeloerythroid progenitors and limited self renewal capability. This cell is Kit-positive, Sca1-positive, CD34-positive, CD150-positive, and is Flt3-negative.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002035 (Slamf1-negative multipotent progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002035 \"A hematopoietic progenitor that has restricted self-renewal capability. Cell is Kit-positive, Ly6-positive, CD150-negative and Flt3-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002035 \"Slamf1-negative multipotent progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002036 (Slamf1-positive multipotent progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002036 \"A hematopoietic progenitor that has some limited self-renewal capability. Cells are lin-negative, Kit-positive, CD34-positive, and Slamf1-positive.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002036 \"Slamf1-positive multipotent progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002043 (CD34-positive, CD38-negative multipotent progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18371405\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19022770\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002043 \"A hematopoietic multipotent progenitor cell that is CD34-positive, CD38-negative, CD45RA-negative, and CD90-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002043 \"Cell markers are associated with human hematopoietic multipotent progenitor cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002043 \"CD34-positive, CD38-negative multipotent progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002044 (Kit-positive, integrin beta7-high basophil mast progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:ak\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002044 \"A basophil mast progenitor cell that is Beta-7 integrin-high, Kit-positive FcRgammaII/III-positive and Sca1-negative.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002044 \"Kit-positive, integrin beta7-high basophil mast progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0517223651\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16824012\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32187560\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WIKIPEDIA:Basal_cell\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:/10.1073/pnas.1734203100\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002187 \"A mitotically active, columnar-shaped keratinocyte located in the stratum basale of the epidermis and attached to the basement membrane. This cell exhibits heterogeneity, encompassing stem and progenitor subpopulations with distinct molecular and proliferative characteristics (Haensel et al., 2020), and serves as the primary source of new keratinocytes for epidermal renewal, homeostasis, and regeneration.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1038/s12276-020-0483-0>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.3389/fcell.2021.644088>) obo:RO_0004050 obo:CL_0002196 \"Liver progenitor cells have been variously named in rodent and human studies as oval cells, hepatic progenitor cells, liver stem cells, ductular reactions, or atypical ductular cells. They were first described as oval cells in rats due to their large nuclear-to-cytoplasm ratio and oval-shaped nuclei. On the difference between 'hepatic liver stem cells' (HLSC) and 'oval cells':  \\\"... unlike a well-known hepatic progenitor cell population, known as oval cells in rodents, HLSCs do not express CK-7, CK-19, c-kit, CD133 and alpha-smooth muscle actin (α-SMA) (Gaudio et al., 2009)\\\".\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(terms:contributor <http://orcid.org/0000-0003-1940-6740>) Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1038/s12276-020-0483-0>) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002196 \"hepatic progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref <https://doi.org/10.1038/s12276-020-0483-0>) oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002196 \"liver progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0721662544\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lens_%28anatomy%29#Lens_epithelium\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002224 \"A cell of the cuboidal epithelium that covers the lens. The cells of the lens epithelium regulate most of the homeostatic functions of the lens. As ions, nutrients, and liquid enter the lens from the aqueous humor, Na+/K+ ATPase pumps in the lens epithelial cells pump ions out of the lens to maintain appropriate lens osmolarity and volume, with equatorially positioned lens epithelium cells contributing most to this current. The activity of the Na+/K+ ATPases keeps water and current flowing through the lens from the poles and exiting through the equatorial regions. The cells of the lens epithelium also serve as the progenitors for new lens fibers. It constantly lays down fibers in the embryo, fetus, infant, and adult, and continues to lay down fibers for lifelong growth.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002287 \"There is debate about the exact lineage of these cell types from this progenitor. See PMID:15738192.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002351 (progenitor cell of endocrine pancreas)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20025937\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20217494\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22728667\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002351 \"A progenitor cell that is able to differentiate into the pancreas alpha, beta and delta endocrine cells. This cell type expresses neurogenin-3 and Isl-1.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002351 \"pancreatic endocrine progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002351 \"pancreatic islet progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002351 \"progenitor cell of endocrine pancreas\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002353 (fetal liver hematopoietic progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002353 \"fetal liver hematopoietic progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002361 (primitive erythroid progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:0813817986\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20711979\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002361 \"A progenitor cell that is capable of forming colonies of primitive erythrocytes in the blood island of the yolk sac. First arrive at E7.5 in mouse and expresses CD41.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002361 \"primitive erythroid progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.3389/fncir.2020.611841\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0002362 \"granule cell progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15580626\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30971890\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35815410\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002375 \"A multipotent progenitor cell that develops from a migratory neural crest cell. The schwann cell precursor is embedded among axons, with minimal extracellular space separating them from nerve cell membranes. This cell lacks a basal lamina, which distinguishes it from more mature Schwann cells. In rodents, cadherin-19 (Cdh19) serves as a specific marker for this developmental stage.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16367798\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20142420\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31583586\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31726662\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37653126\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002453 \"A proliferative and migratory glial progenitor cell that derives from a neural stem cell and resides within the central nervous system. It possesses the capacity to differentiate into a committed oligodendrocyte progenitor (COP) through a well-defined series of maturation steps, ultimately giving rise to a myelinating oligodendrocyte (MOL). In mice and humans, it is characterized by the expression of specific molecular markers, including Pdgfra, Cspg4 (also known as NG2) and Olig2.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"ISBN:9780702028991\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10704434\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2182078\") terms:description obo:CL_0002453 \"This cell type can be purified from optic nerves and other regions of the embryonic, postnatal and adult rat CNS and can be differentiated in vitro to oligodendrocytes and type-2 astrocytes. Some references use the terms 'oligodendrocyte precursor cell' and 'oligodendrocyte type-2 astrocyte (O-2A) progenitor' to refer to the same entity (e.g., PMID:10704434), while others describe an oligodendrocyte type-2 astrocyte (O-2A) progenitor cell as the precurosr to oligodendrocyte- and type-2 astrocyte- progenitor cells (e.g, ISBN:9780702028991).\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002546 (embryonic blood vessel endothelial progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002546 \"An endothelial progenitor cell that participates in angiogenesis during development.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002546 \"embryonic blood vessel endothelial progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002619 (adult endothelial progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20807818\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9020076\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Endothelial_progenitor_cell&oldid=1069930016\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002619 \"An adult angioblastic cell released from the bone marrow, or from the kidney in some teleost species, capable of blood circulation and participation in angiogenesis by differentiating into blood vessel endothelial cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002619 \"The existence of adult endothelial progenitor cells has been controversial in the past.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002619 \"adult endothelial progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24646566\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25843887\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28623666\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34989394\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35343828\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0002623 \"An acinar cell that is part of the salivary gland epithelium, responsible for synthesizing and secreting the primary saliva essential for oral digestion, antimicrobial defense, and mucosal immunity. It features apical-basal polarity with apical secretory granules, and tight junctions that maintain polarity and regulate calcium-dependent saliva exocytosis triggered by parasympathetic and sympathetic signals (Ambudkar, 2015). This cell functions in coordination with contractile myoepithelial cells, which aid saliva flow through the ducts into the oral cavity (Khan et al., 2022). In mice and humans, acinar cell development relies on the transcription factor SOX2 (Emmerson et al., 2017), with self-renewal achieved primarily through acinar cell self-duplication and supported by progenitor populations during injury and regeneration (Aure et al., 2016).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17519333\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19745164\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0002664 \"cardiovascular progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0002672 (retinal progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002672 \"retinal progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005020 \"Lymphatic progenitor cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15624319\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18430230\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005021 \"Mesenchymal derived lymphatic progenitor cells that give rise to the superficial lymphatics.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CL:CVS\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0005022 \"Lymphatic progenitor cells, derived from the veins, that give rise to lymphatic endothelial cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0007010 \"osteoprogenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30827895\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009010 \"transit amplifying progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20801415\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009011 \"A rapidly proliferating population of cells that differentiate from stem cells of the intestinal crypt of the colon. Stem cells located in the crypts of Lieberkühn give rise to proliferating progenitor or transit amplifying cells that differentiate into the four major epithelial cell types. These include columnar absorptive cells or enterocytes, mucous secreting goblet cells, enteroendocrine cells and paneth cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20801415\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-4183-8865\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009012 \"A rapidly proliferating population of cells that differentiate from stem cells of the intestinal crypt of the small intestine. Stem cells located in the crypts of Lieberkühn give rise to proliferating progenitor or transit amplifying cells that differentiate into the four major epithelial cell types. These include columnar absorptive cells or enterocytes, mucous secreting goblet cells, enteroendocrine cells and paneth cells.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009013 (fetal hepatobiliary progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31350390\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3163-0115\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009013 \"A progenitor cell with hepatic and biliary lineage potential, identified in mouse and human, and anatomically restricted to the ductal plate of fetal liver.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009013 \"fetal hepatobiliary hybrid progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009013 \"fetal hepatobiliary progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Endothelial_progenitor_cell&oldid=1069930016#Colony_forming_unit_–_Hill\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009085 \"An adult endothelial progenitor cell characterised in vivo by homing to ischemic sites and paracrine support of angiogenesis. They may form discrete colonies.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Endothelial_progenitor_cell&oldid=1069930016#Circulating_angiogenic_cell\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009088 \"An adult endothelial progenitor cell characterised in vivo by homing to ischemic sites and paracrine support of angiogenesis. These cells do not form colonies.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33419165\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Endothelial_colony_forming_cell&oldid=1068242094\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009090 \"An adult endothelial progenitor cell that is resident of adult vasculature and capable of differentiating to regenerate endothelial cell populations. Endothelial colony forming cells are characterised in vivo by clonal proliferative status, de novo vessel formation, homing to ischemic sites and paracrine support of angiogenesis. These cells are phenotypically similar to endothelial cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21181888\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0002-0819-0473\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009091 \"A stem cell found in the interstitial compartment of the neonatal testis; it is capable of self-renewal as well as differentiation into steroidogenic cells (adult Leydig cells). Intermediate stages of development include progenitor Leydig cells and immature Leydig cells.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009099 (fibro/adipogenic progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20081841\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22045730\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24605102\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009099 \"A progenitor cell that is a tissue-resident mesenchymal cell, important for skeletal muscle regeneration, and able to differentiate into both adipocytes or fibroblasts.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009099 \"fibro/adipogenic progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009099 \"fibro/adipogenic progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0009116 (progenitor cell of mammary luminal epithelium)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:19063729\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20346151\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21930782\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4412-7970\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009116 \"A progenitor cell with the potential to differentiate into luminal epithelial cells of mammary glands. In mouse, CD61 and c-kit were found to be coexpressed by the majority of, but not all, committed luminal progenitor cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0009116 \"luminal progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0009116 \"progenitor cell of luminal mammary epithelium\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0009116 \"progenitor cell of mammary luminal epithelium\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0011020 (neural progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23064725\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30574073\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37508487\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011020 \"An undifferentiated cell derived from a neural stem cell, with a limited capacity to self-renew (Dibajnia and Morshead, 2013) and the ability to generate multiple types of lineage-restricted progenitors, contributing to the formation of neurons, astrocytes, and oligodendrocytes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0011020 \"neural progenitor cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_0011026 (progenitor cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0011026 \"progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41385-022-00565-0\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1000486 \"A basal cell that is part of the urothelium. Compared to other urothelial cell types, a basal cell of the urothelium is positioned along the basement membrane, is the most undifferentiated and serves a progenitor role.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_1001591 (oviduct secretory cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"HPA:HPA\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"NPX:PDR\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_1001591 \"Glandular cell of oviduct epithelium. Example: peg cells, ciliated cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1277\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001591 \"fallopian tube glandular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1277\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001591 \"fallopian tube glandular cells\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001591 \"oviduct glandular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"CALOHA:TS-1277\") oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_1001591 \"uterine tube glandular cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_1001591 \"oviduct secretory cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_4030006 (fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1186/1477-7827-7-129\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.3390/cells8080933\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030006 \"An epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube that secretes mucus and oviduct-specific products in response to hormonal stimulation from estrogen and luteinizing hormone. This fallopian tube secretory cell is similar in height to the ciliated cell, but typically exhibits a more narrow, columnar shape. Its nucleus is ovoid and oriented perpendicular to the cell's long axis, with denser chromatin and a smaller nucleolus compared to the ciliated cell.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"oviduct secretory epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030006 \"uterine tube secretory epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ccr.2013.10.013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/learn/dictionary/normal/fallopian+tube\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4030006 \"The other cell types of the fallopian tube epithelium include the ciliated cell and the intercalary cell, or peg cell. The fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell type has been implicated as a source of high-grade serous ovarian carcinoma.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030006 \"fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_4030007 (fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:16565155\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://www.proteinatlas.org/humanproteome/tissue/fallopian+tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030007 \"A multi-ciliated epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube, mainly found on the apex of the mucosal folds. This cell exhibits a columnar shape with an oval nucleus and is characterized by the presence of cilia on its surface. The coordinated beating of these cilia, together with peristaltic contractions, contributes to the self-propulsion of spermatozoa, the transport of ovum during ovulation and the transport of the fertilized ovum to the intramural fallopian tube.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"oviduct ciliated cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube ciliated cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube multiciliated cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4030007 \"uterine tube ciliated epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4030007 \"fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18757316\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21364219\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34044844\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37834236\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030034 \"A multiciliated epithelial cell located in the respiratory tract epithelium, characterized by a columnar shape and motile cilia on its apical surface. This cell develops through a highly orchestrated process, transitioning from a basal progenitor via an intermediate deuterosomal cell stage that generates centrioles essential for ciliogenesis.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23124355\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4030038 \"After acute tubular injury, this cell type becomes more numerous. In healthy rat kidneys, this cell is not detectable, whereas after unilateral ureteral obstruction (renal injury), it may appear de novo, arguing against the notion that this cell type represents a pre-existing progenitor cell population. In at least one study, data indicate that this cell type represents transiently dedifferentiated tubular cells involved in regeneration.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:17133361\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:24183650\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9374839\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4030066 \"An epithelial cell that is part of a ureteric bud. A ureteric bud cell has the potential to induce metanephric mesenchymal cells to proliferate and convert to epithelia that form renal tubules via: (1) the secretion of multiple diffusible growth factors that rescue renal progenitors from apoptosis and stimulate them to proliferate and (2) contact-dependent mechanisms that induce mesenchymal-epithelial conversion.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2210508\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22911892\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30023181\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033014 \"A small, narrow, peg-shaped epithelial cell with little cytoplasm that is part of oviduct epithelium. This cell is rarer than the ciliated and secretory epithelial cells of the fallopian tube epithelium and is often found intercalated between them. Peg cells are generally distributed basally along the epithelium and have been found in high concentrations at the fimbriated, distal end of the fallopian tube in humans. It may have a regenerative/stem-cell function. In humans, markers include EPCAM, CD44, and ITGA6.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22911892\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033014 \"fallopian tube epithelial stem-like cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25564622\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34044844\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35387001\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37834236\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4033048 \"A respiratory epithelial cell derived from a basal cell, with a topographic nuclear position between the basal and luminal cells of the airway epithelium. This non-basal, intermediate progenitor cell has limited proliferative capacity and can differentiate into multiciliated, secretory, or rare airway cells (ionocytes, tuft cells, neuroendocrine cells). It shares some ultrastructural features with basal cells but lacks the defined characteristics of fully differentiated cellular phenotypes.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25658372\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033048 \"respiratory suprabasal progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26390871\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"alveolar progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2023.04.21.537845\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"luminal progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20346151\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"luminal progenitor cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://nrs.harvard.edu/URN-3:HUL.INSTREPOS:37368328\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4033057 \"ER-negative luminal alveolar progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35091553\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4033059 \"progenitor MEC\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:10467245\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042021 \"A progenitor cell of the central nervous system that differentiates exclusively onto neurons. This progenitor cell is found in a hippocampus subventricular zone, developing cortex and spinal cord of the central nervous system.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12429182\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9354325\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042021 \"In vitro cultures of embryonic mouse neural tubes show that neuronal-restricted precursors (NRPs) are derived from multipotent neuroepithelial cells to give rise to neurons. This progression suggests a linear relationship between multipotent progenitors and neuronal-restricted differentiation. (Mayer-Proschel et al., 1997). In the spinal cord of rats, neural-restricted precursor cells give rise cholinergic, GABAergic, glutametergic neurons (Cao and Howard et al., 2002).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15531362\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33052610\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042022 \"A progenitor cell of the central nervous system that differentiates exclusively onto astrocytes. This progenitor cell expresses CD44 and S100 calcium-binding protein B.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33052610\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4042022 \"In vitro, this progenitor cell can differentiate from glial-restricted precursor cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36148148\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4042026 \"A GABAergic interneuron that has its soma in the anterior section of the substantia nigra pars reticulata. This GABAergic interneuron is characterized by the expression of Six3 and Foxp1 and it develops from Nkx6-2 expressing neuronal progenitors in the ventrolateral midbrain-diencephalon region.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33707780\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35440118\") terms:description obo:CL_4052004 \"Intestinal fibroblastic reticular cells develop from both perivascular and subepithelial progenitors during Peyer's patch formation. Intestinal fibroblastic reticular cells express key markers such as CCL19, CCL21, CXCL13, TNFSF13B (also known as BAFF), and produce IL-7, which are important for their immune regulatory functions and the organization of lymphoid structures.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_4052006 (intestinal enteroendocrine progenitor)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31756561\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasSynonymType obo:OMO_0003000) oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_4052006 \"EEC Progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25670791\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052006 \"The EEC progenitor is also present in other organisms; for example, flies have EEC progenitors but lack intestinal crypts and do not express the same markers. Instead, they are Dl+ and Pros+.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052006 \"intestinal enteroendocrine progenitor\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31320652\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052010 \"progenitor theca cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15833266\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31320652\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32530882\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Theca_interna\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052012 \"A specialized theca cell that forms the inner, highly vascularized layer of the theca surrounding ovarian follicles. Originating from progenitor theca cells, the theca interna cell is steroidogenic, playing a crucial role in the production of androgens, which serves as a precursor for estrogen synthesis in granulosa cells. This cell expresses luteinizing hormone receptors, enabling it to respond to hormonal signals that regulate steroidogenesis.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31320652\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32530882\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36758341\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Theca_externa\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052013 \"A specialized theca cell that forms the outer layer of the theca surrounding the ovarian follicle, appearing at the antral follicle. Originating from progenitor theca cells, theca externa cell is characterized by its fibroblast-like appearance and primarily function to provide structural support to the developing follicle. This cell produces collagen fibers and extracellular matrix components such as Col1a1 and Col1a2.\")\n# Class: obo:CL_4052018 (fallopian tube epithelial cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Fallopian_tube\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052018 \"Any epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Fallopian_tube\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4052018 \"oviduct epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"Wikipedia:Fallopian_tube\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052018 \"uterine tube epithelial cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052018 \"fallopian tube epithelial cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_4052019 (fallopian tube non-ciliated epithelial cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052019 \"Any epithelial cell that is part of the fallopian tube and lacks cilia.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052019 \"fallopian tube non-ciliated cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052019 \"fallopian tube non-ciliated epithelial cell\")\n# Class: obo:CL_4052022 (fallopian tube smooth muscle cell)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31183831\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613440\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4052022 \"A smooth muscle cell that is part of the fallopian tube. This cell is responsible for peristaltic contractions that facilitate gamete and embryo transport, fluid mixing, and embryo admission to the uterus.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613440\") oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_4052022 \"oviduct smooth muscle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31613440\") oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_4052022 \"uterine tube smooth muscle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18621753\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052022 \"The fallopian tube smooth muscle cell in the human contracts dynamically in response to hormones and signaling molecules. Prostaglandins, particularly PGF2α and PGE2, have been shown to increase muscular contractions, while progesterone, levonorgestrel, mifepristone, oxytocin, and human chorionic gonadotropin (hCG) decrease them. These contractile responses are crucial for regulating gamete and embryo transport through the fallopian tube.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4052022 \"fallopian tube smooth muscle cell\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35355013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36796082\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_4052031 \"The respiratory airway secretory cell is cuboidal and has a unique transcriptomic profile compared to other epithelial cells in the same region. In humans, it functions as a multipotent progenitor, capable of regenerating alveolar type 2 (AT2) cells.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27284195\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30837646\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39233334\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9473608\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4072002 \"A postmitotic and differentiated oligodendrocyte derived from a oligodendrocyte progenitor cell. A myelin-forming oligodendrocyte begins the expression of myelin genes and actively engages in the myelination process. In mice and humans, it is characterized by the upregulation of the key myelin-associated markers Mbp and Opalin. Additionally, Ctps (CTP synthase) shows peak expression at this stage, suggesting a heightened demand for nucleotide biosynthesis during membrane expansion and myelin production.\")\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
