{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,220p' PR_COMMENTS.md && sed -n '1,80p' ISSUE_COMMENTS.md\"","aggregated_output":"## Summary\n\nAdded a new CL term, `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell`, for issue #3196.\n\n## Rationale\n\nThe issue discussion settled on `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell` as the preferred label instead of the historical \"unclassified\" label. I used `progenitor cell` as the genus, placed the term in the human fallopian tube epithelium with `part of some UBERON:8600124` and `in taxon some NCBITaxon:9606`, and modeled the reviewed epithelial differentiation capacity with `develops into` restrictions to fallopian tube secretory epithelial cell and fallopian tube multiciliated epithelial cell.\n\nI used `UBERON:8600124` because it is the direct Uberon term for fallopian tube epithelium; `UBERON:0007589` is narrower ciliated columnar oviduct epithelium.\n\n## Completed Checklist\n\n- Checked the issue context and comments.\n- Checked for existing matching CL terms/synonyms in `src/ontology/cl-edit.owl`.\n- Checked proposed parent context for `CL:4052018`, `CL:4052019`, `CL:4030006`, `CL:4030007`, and `CL:0011026`.\n- Checked relevant DOSDP patterns for cell part-of anatomical entity and taxon-specific modeling.\n- Reviewed PMID:40475517 and PMID:35320732 metadata/content available locally or via web access.\n- Added PMID-backed definition and synonyms.\n- Added contributor ORCID and term tracker item annotation.\n- Ran `robot convert -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -o /tmp/cl-edit.ofn`.\n- Ran `robot reason -i src/ontology/cl-edit.owl -r ELK -o /tmp/cl-reasoned.owl`.\n- Ran `git diff --check`.\n\nSigned-off-by: GitHub Copilot\nChanges committed in PR #<NN>.\n\nAdded `dual-feature fallopian tube progenitor cell` as requested, using the reviewed label, definition, synonyms, and logical definition from the issue discussion.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
